[82.0176, "o", "\r\n"]
[82.2676, "o", "fix(deploy): use decimal multipliers for the M and G quantity suffixes\r\n\r\nReview fixes for the Kubernetes quantity parser:\r\n\r\n- quantity.py: `M` and `G` were powers of 1024, so parse_quantity(\"1M\")\r\n  returned 1048576 and memory_bytes(\"1G\") returned 1073741824. Kubernetes,\r\n  the module docstring and the PR description all define them as powers\r\n  of 1000. They now are. Prompted by a CodeRabbit review thread.\r\n- test_quantity.py: add regression cases for `1M`, `1G` and\r\n  memory_bytes(\"1G\"); all three fail on the previous multipliers.\r\n\r\nAutomated-by: pr-shepherd\r\nCo-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>\r\nSigned-off-by: Jonathan Tong <jt572@cornell.edu>\r\n\r\ndeploy/utils/quantity.py  +2 -2\r\ndeploy/utils/tests/test_quantity.py  +3 -0\r\n"]
